     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. At that dose, serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity are real risks. A 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function has no physiologic reason to tolerate it.\n\nYou're the prescriber, and I'm not questioning your authority. But I can't be the one to put an order this far outside safe limits into the system.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter up to 200 mg once daily right away. Titration could be gradual, for example 50 mg and then increasing.\n- **Consult pharmacy or psychiatry.** If you think the patient needs more than the labeled maximum, they can review it with you.\n- **Enter it yourself.** If you still believe this dose is warranted, you can place the order directly through the standard system. That route will trigger pharmacy verification and dose-limit alerts.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter one of the in-range doses."
      }
     ],
